  "summary": "Zenith Technology (ZenTech), a Dunedin, New Zealand provider of clinical trial and analytical laboratory services, was hit by a ransomware attack attributed to the ZaWoo group around August 2026. Data held by ZenTech included Coroners Court information for Otago/Southland cases from 2016-2022 held for the Ministry of Justice, plus patient and clinical trial data. On August 31, 2026 ZaWoo posted samples of patient data (names, addresses, blood test results) and demanded a ransom in bitcoin. A High Court injunction restricted access to the data.",
